{"duration_api_ms":53927,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"0204548c-a824-57b7-bea3-1783011bc81a","total_cost_usd":0.4266742,"usage":{"input_tokens":18,"cache_creation_input_tokens":27066,"cache_read_input_tokens":463271,"output_tokens":5871,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":261},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":27066,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":912,"cache_read_input_tokens":58615,"cache_creation_input_tokens":821,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":821},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":18,"outputTokens":5871,"cacheReadInputTokens":463271,"cacheCreationInputTokens":27066,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.4266742,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":261,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":27066,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01KHevjjNhdjD4wXhG5ZBTE3","tool_input":{"command":"cd Common/sources; wc -l *.js storage/*.js | sort -n | tail -15; git log --since=90.days --oneline -- . | wc -l; git log --oneline -- . | wc -l; ls ../../tests/unit; grep -l \"require('.*Common\" -r ../../DocService/sources ../../FileConverter/sources 2>/dev/null | wc -l; git rev-parse --short HEAD; grep -n \"readFile\\|parse\\|ssrf\\|SSRF\" utils.js | head -8"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01RDpBaFZRnhTzwHxEvh5Kmw","tool_input":{"command":"f=$(ls .theseus/queue/in-progress/PKT-0004-*.md); python3 - \"$f\" <<'EOF'\nimport sys;p=sys.argv[1];s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"## Executor log\\n\",\"\"\"## Executor log\n- Verdict: refactor (JS + gradual @ts-check), wave 0 = characterize tenantManager, operationContext, storage-base; wave 1 = JSDoc type-check and break utils/operationContext cycle.\n- Decision: did not choose migrate to TypeScript: uncovered parts are exactly what it would touch; D3 double diagnosis avoided by not needing it yet.\n- Surprise: git history restarted (1 commit touches Common), so churn is unusable as evidence; no graph.json, coupling estimated by grep (27 consumer files).\n- Not done: friction.jsonl entry not written, to stay within target.create_in (.theseus/diagnosis) and the 2-file budget.\n\"\"\",1)\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s)\nEOF\ntest -s .theseus/diagnosis/DIAG-common.md && echo OK; git add -A .theseus && git commit -qm \"docs(diagnosis): diagnose common module as refactor\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GfMVS4GJ2FBm26wB5X9Aot\" && git log --oneline -1"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":10,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"My verdict for the `common` module is **refactor**: stay in JavaScript, write tests for the untested parts first, then make small structural fixes. The verdict is in `.theseus/diagnosis/DIAG-common.md`, the acceptance check passes, and the work is committed as `821f3bd`.\n\n**Why refactor:**\n- **Security and coupling:** Common is used by DocService, FileConverter, AdminPanel and SpellChecker. 27 files in DocService and FileConverter alone require it. It also handles the server's most sensitive logic: download filtering against SSRF, JWT helpers, tenant resolution from the Host header, and keeping each tenant's storage keys separate.\n- **Maintenance:** `utils.js` is 1,563 lines of mixed concerns, `commondefines.js` is 1,245 lines, and `utils`, `operationContext` and `tenantManager` require each other in a cycle.\n- **Thin tests:** `tenantManager`, `operationContext`, storage and the task queues have no unit tests.\n\n**Why not migrate to TypeScript yet:** the untested parts are exactly what a migration would touch, and the many consumers plus the require cycle would make a mixed JS/TS build costly. Adding `// @ts-check` with JSDoc types gets most of the type-safety benefit without changing the build. I recorded what would change this: if the new tests raise the oracle to `good` and type checking finds real bugs, the module should be reassessed as migrate. That would need a second, independent diagnosis from another model.\n\n**Packet plan** (the machine-readable block is in the verdict file):\n\n| Key | Wave | Type | Work |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| P1 | 0 | characterize | Tests for `tenantManager` |\n| P2 | 0 | characterize | Tests for `operationContext` |\n| P3 | 0 | characterize | Tests for `storage-base` using the file-system backend |\n| P4 | 1 | refactor | `@ts-check` and JSDoc types on `commondefines` and `operationContext` |\n| P5 | 1 | refactor | Break the `utils` ↔ `operationContext` require cycle |\n\n**Not done:** I didn't add the `friction.jsonl` entry that AGENTS.md asks for. That file is outside this packet's `create_in`, so it needs to be written outside this packet. The Executor log in the packet is filled in.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas:**\n- The git history was restarted, so only one commit touches Common and churn tells us nothing. The verdict leans on code size and coupling instead.\n- There is no `graph.json`, so I estimated coupling with grep. The card's dependency fields stay empty until the graph tool runs.","ttft_ms":2191,"type":"result","duration_ms":55017,"uuid":"9c8db565-5182-4e16-bc1b-585b30ead453","ttft_stream_ms":1139,"time_to_request_ms":524,"time_to